#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Look and Feel</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "Force smaller tool view tabs in IDEAl Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default &kdevelop; starts with large text-based tool tip tabs around the "
"work area. You may change this look to &eg; save space in the &kdevelop; "
"configuration dialog (<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure KDevelop...</guimenuitem> <guimenuitem>User "
"Interface</guimenuitem></menuchoice>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:42
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use an older &kdevelop; 3 version, this configuration dialog may not "
"be available. To change the toolview tabs display manually, place a "
"<option>MDIStyle</option> entry under the <option>[UI]</option> tag in your "
"<filename>$KDEHOME/share/config/kdeveloprc</filename> configuration file as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: nutshell.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>MDIStyle=0</option>: icons only"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: nutshell.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>MDIStyle=1</option>: text only (default)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: nutshell.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "<option>MDIStyle=3</option>: icons and text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Weird colored characters and/or display style"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you notice random colored letters everywhere (&ie; on tabs, on tool bars, "
"etc.) and the &kdevelop; window seemingly uses a wrong display style, this "
"may help:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In your <filename>$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/share/config/kdeveloprc</filename> "
"configuration file find the line containing "
"<quote><computeroutput>Style=Checked</computeroutput></quote> and remove it. "
"Then restart &kdevelop;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"(This behaviour does sometimes occur after you left clicked a .ui file in "
"one of the file navigators and &kdevelop; did load <application>KUIViewer</"
"application> to show the &GUI; which was produced from this file.)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Full screen mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Full-Screen Mode</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menus or press <keycombo>&Ctrl;&Shift;"
"<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide/Unhide the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To hide the menubar select <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Menubar</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menus "
"or press <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo>. To redisplay the "
"menubar only <keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap> </keycombo> is available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: nutshell.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Projects</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create New Project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Project</guimenu><guimenuitem>New Project...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> will start the <link linkend=\"applicationwizard"
"\">&appwizard;</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create a custom project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is no direct way to create a custom project (&ie; a project which does "
"use its own makefiles). Use <menuchoice><guimenu>Project</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Import Existing Project</guimenuitem></menuchoice> instead. "
"Remember to set the appropriate <guilabel>Project Type</guilabel>, labeled "
"by an additional <quote>(Custom Makefiles)</quote>, in the dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use project options early"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Whenever you start a new project do not forget to set the "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Project Options...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> to your needs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: nutshell.docbook:139
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Compilation</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "Missing detail in compilation messages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If during compilations you notice some valuable information is missing in "
"the <guilabel>Messages Output View</guilabel> window, it may be that the "
"level of message detail is set too low. &RMB; click in the window and select "
"another detail level from the context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "Create new files in a project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the sub-project in the upper half of the &automanag;, then &RMB; "
"click in the lower half on the groups title you want to have the files added "
"and select <guimenuitem>Create New File...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add existing files to a project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the sub-project in the upper half of the &automanag;, then &RMB; "
"click in the lower half on the groups title you want to have the files added "
"and select <guimenuitem>Add Existing Files...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove a file from a project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the sub-project in the upper half of the &automanag;, then in the "
"lower half open the groups list you want to have the file removed from, "
"&RMB; click on the file in this list and select <guimenuitem>Remove</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: nutshell.docbook:189
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Compile/Make Problems</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project does not build again after switching to/from default target"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a problem with the &automake;/&autoconf; machinery. If <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Build Configuration</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> provides to select from three build directories: "
"<guimenuitem>default</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>optimized</guimenuitem>, "
"and <guimenuitem>debug</guimenuitem>, by all means stick to "
"<emphasis>either</emphasis> the default <emphasis>or</emphasis> the debug/"
"optimized targets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you configured your project with default it will no longer build with "
"debug or optimzed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once you configured your project with debug or optimzed it will no longer "
"build with default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: nutshell.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "<quote>Wrong <command>autoconf</command> version</quote> &etc; Error"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are several error messages concerning too old versions of "
"<application>autoconf</application> &etc; prohibiting <command>configure</"
"command> to work properly. Run <command>autoreconf</command> in the "
"directory tree where the <filename>configure.in</filename> files in question "
"are. This command will try to update the information in the &GNU; Build "
"System files. See <command>man autoreconf</command> for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: nutshell.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Other Topics</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: link
#: nutshell.docbook:233
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration Files used by &kdevelop;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: nutshell.docbook:236
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Usually you should not need to care, but this is very useful to know in case "
"something went wrong with your setup."
msgstr ""
